# PadicFamiliesPartII: target signatures

The roadmap is README.md; this file is not the roadmap. It states the roadmap's
headline theorems against the pinned Mathlib and Tau Ceti APIs whenever their
carriers are available. None of the following headlines is statable at these pins:

* PEL small-slope classicality (Layer 2, §2.8) lacks PEL Shimura varieties at
  Iwahori level, their rigid generic fibres, the automorphic sheaves ω^κ,
  overconvergent sections and the normalized U_i correspondences.
* Spherical singular-weight amplitude and the vanishing Euler characteristic of
  the localized Klingen family (Layer 3, §§3.3 and 3.5) lack the Siegel threefold
  with its toroidal and minimal compactifications, coherent cohomology of
  Sym^k ω ⊗ det(ω)^r (−D), the integral Hecke correspondences at p and the
  one-variable Klingen Iwasawa complex.
* Hilbert–Siegel partial-ordinary derived control (Layer 4, §4.7) lacks
  Hilbert–Siegel varieties at mixed Klingen/Iwahori level, partial Igusa towers,
  the universal coefficient sheaf and its derived global sections over Λ_I.
* The weight-two doubling injection and its unit-root refinements (Layer 5,
  §§5.8–5.9) lack the special fibres of these varieties, the partial Frobenius,
  and the sections of ω^(2,2)(−D) on the mixed rank and w-ordinary loci.
* Multi-place small-slope continuation and the one-place rational comparison
  (Layer 6, §§6.5 and 6.7) lack the analytic Hilbert–Siegel coefficient sheaves,
  overconvergent coherent cohomology and the Hida complex M_I.
* The higher Eichler–Shimura spectral sequence and the genus-two four-piece
  filtration (Layer 7, §§7.3 and 7.6) lack completed cohomology of Shimura
  towers, derived locally analytic vectors, the BGG category O(𝔤,𝔟), analytic
  localization on the flag variety and higher Coleman cohomology.
* The Sen–Cousin comparison and de Rham classicality at the singular weight
  (Layer 8, §§8.4 and 8.6) lack, in addition, the arithmetic Sen operator on
  completed cohomology and Galois representations attached to its Hecke
  eigensystems.
* The four finite projective Hida modules, their classical and higher Coleman
  specializations, integral duality and tame group-ring projectivity (Layer 9)
  lack the universal supported Iwasawa complexes of Siegel threefolds and the
  coherent cohomology they specialize to.

The companion operator of §5.6 and the numerical slope conditions of §§2.1 and
6.5 are elementary, but they are not headline theorems and are not needed to
state any headline; they stay in README.md as targets and Checks.
-/

